("h3", "Reaction with acids"),
("p", "Metal + dilute acid &rarr; salt + hydrogen. Mg + 2HCl &rarr; MgCl<sub>2</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>. Fe + 2HCl &rarr; FeCl<sub>2</sub> + H<sub>2</sub>. Copper, silver and gold do not react with dilute HCl. **Nitric acid** is a strong oxidising agent and generally does not give hydrogen. **Aqua regia** (3 parts conc. HCl and 1 part conc. HNO<sub>3</sub>) dissolves gold and platinum."),
