("table", ["Reactivity", "Examples", "Method"], [["High (above Al, including Al)", "K, Na, Ca, Mg, Al", "Electrolytic reduction of molten chloride or oxide: at the cathode Na<sup>+</sup> + e<sup>&minus;</sup> &rarr; Na"], ["Medium", "Zn, Fe, Pb", "Convert to oxide (roasting of sulphide or calcination of carbonate), then reduce with carbon"], ["Low", "Cu, Hg, Ag, Au", "Cinnabar is heated: 2HgS + 3O<sub>2</sub> &rarr; 2HgO + 2SO<sub>2</sub>; 2HgO &rarr; 2Hg + O<sub>2</sub>; Cu<sub>2</sub>S gives copper on heating in air"]]),
("ul", ["**Roasting:** strong heating of a sulphide ore in excess air: 2ZnS + 3O<sub>2</sub> &rarr; 2ZnO + 2SO<sub>2</sub>.", "**Calcination:** strong heating of a carbonate ore in limited air: ZnCO<sub>3</sub> &rarr; ZnO + CO<sub>2</sub>.", "**Reduction with carbon:** ZnO + C &rarr; Zn + CO.", "**Thermite reaction:** Fe<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> + 2Al &rarr; Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub> + 2Fe + heat; the molten iron is used to weld railway tracks. 3MnO<sub>2</sub> + 4Al &rarr; 3Mn + 2Al<sub>2</sub>O<sub>3</sub>."]),
